    // megler-w10m: members added to the original's android.os.MessageQueue (tools/build-framework.sh, "X.java.members").
    // next(), Android's own name for what Looper.loop takes the next message with: blocks until one is due, null once the
    // queue has quit. It is hidden API, and code that runs its own event loop takes the Java looper's messages with it:
    // Gecko's (Firefox 152) asks for it by JNI on the Gecko thread, and without it ended on a NoSuchMethodError
    // (MOZ_CRASH()) as it started. The original has only next(boolean main), which this calls as Looper.loop does.
    Message next() { return next(Looper.getMainLooper() != null && Looper.getMainLooper().getQueue() == this); }
